prompt:
Signup needs a username check. Add is_valid_username(name) to accounts/usernames.py that returns True or False (it never raises). It is called on names that have already gone through normalize_username, and a name is valid when all of these hold:

- it is a str of 3 to 20 characters, inclusive;
- it starts with a lowercase ASCII letter (a-z);
- every character is a lowercase ASCII letter, an ASCII digit, or one of the separators ".", "_" and "-" (so uppercase, spaces, other symbols and non-ASCII letters are all invalid);
- two separators never appear next to each other, in any combination ("a..b", "a._b" and "a-.b" are all invalid);
- it does not end with a separator.

Anything that isn't a str returns False. Reserved names are handled separately by is_reserved, so don't check them here.
